# Copy to `.env` for local development, and set the same variable in your
# hosting provider's environment for deploys. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# NOT prefixed VITE_, and that is the whole point: Vite inlines every VITE_*
# variable into the client bundle at build time, so a key named
# VITE_FOURSQUARE_... would be shipped to every visitor. This one is read only
# by the serverless function in api/place.ts and by the dev middleware in
# vite.config.ts, both of which run in Node and never hand it to the browser.
#
# Setup: foursquare.com/developers -> create a project -> generate a Service
# Key. The free tier needs no card.
#
# The key is sent as `Authorization: Bearer <key>` to
# places-api.foursquare.com, together with a pinned `X-Places-Api-Version`
# header. Both were confirmed by probing the live API — see the note at the top
# of server/placeLookup.ts.
#
# Leave it unset and the app still works: /api/place answers "no result" and
# every lookup falls back to Nominatim, exactly as before this endpoint existed.
FOURSQUARE_API_KEY=
